 34S     4HE(30SI,A):RES:XUNDL-2       2011NO07                           201108
 34S  c  Compiled (unevaluated) data set from 2011No07:                         
 34S 2c  Eur Phys J  A 47, 73 (2011)                                            
 34S  c  Compiled by M. Birch and B. Singh (McMaster); July 31, 2011.           
 34S  c  {+30}Si+|a resonance experiment performed at the K-130 cyclotron at the
 34S 2c  university of Jyvaskyla, Finland. {+30}Si beam, E=150 MeV entered      
 34S 3c  scattering chamber of helium gas through Havar foil. Recoiling         
 34S 4c  |a-particles detected by rotating array of four silicon surface        
 34S 5c  detectors as well as another detector which was fixed. Time-of-flight  
 34S 6c  measured using the cyclotron Rf signal. Deduced excitation function,   
 34S 7c  levels, and widths. R-matrix analysis of excitation function data      
 34S  cL $ Only the excitations observed in the present work are given here     
 34S  cL $ Relative reduced widths=|g{+2}{-|a}/|g{+2}{-sp} are given in percent 
 34S  cL E$ 2011No07 state an uncertainty of |?100 keV in the absolute energy   
 34S 2cL calibration                                                            
 34S  CL T$LABEL=WIDTH                                                          
 34S  cL T$ Widths reported are only an upper limit due to probable             
 34S 2cL overestimation of |G{-|a}/|G resulting from the experimental setup,    
 34S 3cL which is especially pronounced for the lowest resonance measured and   
 34S 4cL less of a factor at the higher energies. 2011No07 estimate a mean      
 34S 5cL overestimation of 30%.                                                 
